    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_5cc8b6c2",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: spot_the_difference_monkeys; hasOverallIntent: harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a large group of baboons, many with open mouths, in a crowded scene, with the text 'spot the difference' overlaid. The visual content is not inherently abusive or hateful toward any specific group, but the meme format relies on the viewer's engagement with the image. The potential harm arises from the historical and cultural context of comparing humans to primates, which has been used in racist stereotypes to demean Black people. Although the image itself does not contain explicit racist imagery, the juxtaposition of the text 'spot the difference' with the image of monkeys can unintentionally reinforce or normalize the dehumanizing trope of equating humans with animals, particularly when such comparisons are historically used to justify discrimination. The meme's intent is to create a playful challenge, but its potential to perpetuate harmful analogies makes it harmful in context.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_dfce7a70"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
